 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+6 & 0-2 & 10+0 \\\\ -8-4 & 4+1 & 0-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -12 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6727fdd-a614-5ead-9273-08c0a7fec997" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43f31230-0191-5a33-9bb6-0fa7b614f351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 15 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 14 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392961} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc9309-5767-5a6f-9aa6-d329adc4d01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392962} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8254f-ba83-5a63-900a-3e1c1e498e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\